{"updated_at": {"date": {"d": "20", "m": "08", "Y": "2026"}, "time": {"H": "08", "M": "22", "S": "37"}}, "news": [{"title": "Water crisis hits 4,338 Taloja flats, Navi Mumbai residents protest outside Cidco Bhawan", "para": "Asawari Gruhasankul residents protested Cidco Bhawan over persistent water scarcity issues.  They demanded adequate potable water supply for their 4,338 apartments.  Residents expressed frustration with poor quality tanker water and daily bottled water expenses.  Cidco authorities promised to resolve the water crisis within fifteen to twenty days.  They also stated that booster pump usage by societies would face legal action.", "href": "https://realty.economictimes.indiatimes.com/news/residential/water-crisis-hits-4338-taloja-flats-navi-mumbai-residents-protest-outside-cidco-bhawan/133367373?utm_source=newslisting&utm_medium=latestNews", "img": "data:image/png;base64, ", "img-src": "https://etimg.etb2bimg.com/thumb/img-size-208922/133367373.cms?width=150&height=112", "tag": "residential"}, {"title": "Gujarat: Popular Builders owner Dashrath Patel denied bail in two cases", "para": "A sessions court has refused bail to Dashrath Patel, the owner of Popular Builders, in connection with two land grabbing allegations. His brother, Raman Patel, is serving a four-year prison term for a related Chekhla land case. Both have been charged with forgery and cheating linked to land deals. The court's decision reflects concerns about potential witness tampering and has significant implications for their ongoing legal battle.", "href": "https://realty.economictimes.indiatimes.com/news/regulatory/gujarat-popular-builders-owner-dashrath-patel-denied-bail-in-two-cases/133367250?utm_source=newslisting&utm_medium=latestNews", "img": "data:image/png;base64, ", "img-src": "https://etimg.etb2bimg.com/thumb/img-size-109691/133367250.cms?width=150&height=112", "tag": "regulatory"}, {"title": "DLF-3 residents in Gurugram seek policy for workforce housing amid razing", "para": "Residents of DLF-3 organized a large meeting to voice their demands for a housing policy that benefits local workers. They protested against government actions of sealing and demolitions that jeopardize accommodation for the workforce. Advocating for the right to remedy property violations through payments, they emphasized the need for a comprehensive legal framework encompassing guest and rental housing options.", "href": "https://realty.economictimes.indiatimes.com/news/residential/dlf-3-residents-in-gurugram-seek-policy-for-workforce-housing-amid-razing/133364187?utm_source=newslisting&utm_medium=latestNews", "img": "data:image/png;base64, ", "img-src": "https://etimg.etb2bimg.com/thumb/img-size-431194/133364187.cms?width=150&height=112", "tag": "residential"}]}